# perf-workspace.ux.nt — the seed that makes a graph named `perf` open to the bench dashboard (la Lente, 2026-10-25).
#
# The SAME mechanism the `observatory` graph uses (see observatory-workspace.ux.nt): a sux:Workspace whose
# region-center is rendered by the `sh-layout-dashboard` fragment marker, plus a ux:layoutJson LayoutDocument on the
# region's sux:fragmentSurface. Here the fragment is ONE leaf: the `bench.dashboard` face (packages/runtime/src/layout/
# faces/bench-dashboard-face.ts) over resource {kind:graph, graphId:"perf"}. The face reads the ledger with the
# GRAPH-wrapped SPARQL of bench-model.ts; it writes nothing.
#
# APPLY at seed time, not build time, like the Observatory seed: insert these triples into the perf cell's
# `:ux:config` named graph, urn:mnemosyne:local:graph:perf:ux:config, e.g.
#   ~/.sophia-mcp/sirin-call.sh perf rdf_load '{"target_graph_iri":"urn:mnemosyne:local:graph:perf:ux:config","data":"<this file>","format":"ntriples"}'
# (check `rdf_load`'s exact argument names with the tool schema; the mechanism, not the spelling, is the point).
# Then open the graph: `?graph=perf`.
#
# The layout document's `graphId` is the cell's own graph id, "perf". If the ledger graph has another id, change it in
# BOTH places (the literal's graphId and resource.graphId) or re-author the literal. The workspace config also
# carries the usual top bar and an optional chat rail.
